/* book Worked example: Q: A 3 m steel cantilever, fixed at x = 0, carries w = 4 kN/m. E = 200 GPa, I = 12 × 10⁻⁶ m⁴. Find free-end deflection by unit load and check.
   1. x from fixed end, sagging positive. The load is hogging: M(x) = −w(L−x)²/2 = −2(3−x)² kN·m.
   2. Remove load; put 1 kN downward at x = 3 m. m(x) = −(3−x) kN·m per kN.
   3. M m = 2(3−x)³ kN·m² per kN; minus signs cancel, so positive means downward.
   4. EI = 200×10⁹×12×10⁻⁶ = 2.4×10⁶ N·m² = 2400 kN·m². ∫₀³ 2(3−x)³ dx = 40.5 kN·m³.
   5. Δ = 40.5/2400 = 0.016875 m. Check: wL⁴/(8EI) = 4×81/(8×2400) = 0.016875 m.
   Answer: Δ = 0.016875 m = 16.875 mm, downward at the free end, matching wL⁴/(8EI). */
