/* book: lead: A beam with more reactions than equilibrium can solve is statically indeterminate. The force method turns one unknown reaction into the subject of a single equation. Remove that reaction and the beam becomes determinate; the real loads then push the freed point away from its support. Put the reaction back as an unknown force R; it pushes the point back. The two movements must cancel, and that one  */
